drm/virtio: no MOVE_CURSOR when the cursor did not move

LP-only. virtio_gpu_cursor_plane_update() sends the host a MOVE_CURSOR
whenever the cursor plane is part of an atomic commit and its FB did not
change - also when its position did not change either. wlroots puts the
cursor plane in every commit, so every frame of the screen came with a
cursor "move" to where the cursor already was, and under QEMU with SPICE
each one went on to the viewer through SPICE's cursor channel. A commit
that leaves the cursor where it is now sends nothing for it.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_plane.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_plane.c
@@ -374,6 +374,16 @@
 			output->cursor.hot_y = cpu_to_le32(0);
 		}
 	} else {
+		/*
+		 * LP: the same image at the same place is not a move. A
+		 * compositor that puts the cursor plane in every atomic commit
+		 * (wlroots) otherwise sends the host a MOVE_CURSOR with every
+		 * frame of the screen, and SPICE forwards each one to the
+		 * viewer.
+		 */
+		if (plane->state->crtc_x == old_state->crtc_x &&
+		    plane->state->crtc_y == old_state->crtc_y)
+			return;
 		DRM_DEBUG("move +%d+%d\n",
 			  plane->state->crtc_x,
 			  plane->state->crtc_y);
